# Diablo II Data Manifest

Source: Diablo II: Resurrected (D2R)
Base Patch: 2.7 (Build 2.7.3.77443)
Extraction Date: 2023-06-15

## Extracted Game Data Tables (data/d2r/)

Raw TSV tables extracted from Blizzard CASC game storage:
- Armor.txt, Weapons.txt, Misc.txt (base item equipment definitions and categories)
- ItemStatCost.txt (stat identifiers, save bits, save add offsets, and value shifts)
- Properties.txt (property identifiers mapped to stat IDs and calculation formulas)
- itemtypes.txt (item type taxonomy, inheritance hierarchy, body locations, beltability)
- magicprefix.txt, magicsuffix.txt (magical affix definitions and stat ranges)
- uniqueitems.txt (unique item definitions and property assignments)
- setitems.txt (set item definitions, item indices, and stat ranges)
- runes.txt (runeword compositions, sockets, and rune requirements)
- gems.txt (gem and rune socket modifiers for weapons, armor, and shields)
- skills.txt (character and monster skill definitions, aura identifiers)

## Localized String Tables (data/d2r/local/)

JSON localized string tables extracted from D2R localization archives:
- item-modifiers.json, skills.json, item-names.json, item-nameaffixes.json
- item-gems.json, item-runes.json, monsters.json, npcs.json, quests.json
- shrines.json, levels.json, objects.json, mercenaries.json, commands.json
- keybinds.json, tooltip-ui.json, ui.json

## Version Overlay (data/0x63/)

Overlay files for D2R Beta / v1.0.0 (version 0x63 / 99) save compatibility:
- Armor.txt, ItemStatCost.txt, Misc.txt, Weapons.txt, itemtypes.txt
- itemdata.txt, property.txt

## Generated / Hand-Maintained Parsing Files

- itemdata.txt: Compact bitstream parser metadata specifying item classification flags
  (simple, charm, defense, durability, stackable). Hand-maintained in repository; original
  generator script referenced in legacy README.py was not committed to version control.
- property.txt: Property unpack descriptors specifying bit widths, bias offsets, and version
  thresholds for variable-length property decoding. Hand-maintained in repository.
